# Grid and stack layout cards

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

A layout card does not show any information itself. It holds other cards and arranges them: in a grid, side by side or one above another. Use one to keep related cards together, such as the readings and controls for one room.

For where layout fits in a whole dashboard, see [Dashboard composition and card features](../home-assistant/dashboard-composition.html).

This page covers:

- Grid and stack layout cards
  - `hui-grid-card`
  - `hui-horizontal-stack-card`
  - `hui-vertical-stack-card`

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

All three have the same parts: an optional title, then the cards they hold. The title is drawn as a level 1 heading inside the card, with padding above and below. The layout card has no border or background of its own, so each card inside keeps its own.

The cards inside are read in the order they appear in the `cards` list. A horizontal stack or a grid changes where they sit on the screen, not the reading order.

